'm not been a huge David  Lynch obsessed kind of fan I've always  enjoyed his work I think he's great I  think that he approaches moviemaking as  an artist approaches making visual art  or a musician making music and I think  it's really refreshing most of the time  the thing about Twin Peaks was I didn't  watch TV when it came out at all like  I'd you know nobody really did I was a  teenager it came out in 1990 so I was in  my senior year of high school so I was  about the age of the people that were in  the show there was a lot of hype about  it I did know David Lynch I knew this  was an interesting thing and what really  got me into it was an older kid I knew  was talking about it and you know I'm  not really sure if he hadn't if I really  would have watched it when it first came  out really enjoyed fire walk with me  when it first came out I was more into  movies and TV shows think pretty much  everybody was the quality of movies was  a lot higher than TV was at that time  core Twin Peaks paid a big part in that  changing over the last couple decades  but yeah look when Peaks open the door  to re watching and re watching over the  years  definitely watch season one more than  season two but both of them are good  although season two definitely has its  problems but we're gonna do season one  here one see how it goes and then if it  does if it you know probably if the  patreon still going and there's still  interest then we will go straight  through season two as well I do have to  mention the music in season one after  watching season three which I loved and  I mean obviously you can  compared both because seasons 1 &amp; 2 were  made at a different time when nothing  like that at all was on TV so of course  season 3 would be different but I  probably like season 3 the best out of  all of them but the music in season 1 &amp;  2 is just amazingly cool it's like an  extra character in the scenes I think  sometimes and even though we got it in  smaller doses in season 3 I really enjoy  the saturation of the music in season 1  and season 2 so in the next installment  which will be following sometime next  week I guess we'll get to see an episode  that Lynch and Frost wrote but David  Lynch did not direct there's a different  director so we'll see how that holds up  until then thanks for watching guys I'll  talk to you soon
 

